9  An analysis of the aforesaid directives would indicate the following procedure to be adopted in the matter of retesting of samples:-
 (a) Upon tests of initial samples being completed, results of such tests are  to be furnished to all parties, that is, prosecution and the accused (if  available);
 (b) A request for retesting must be made by any party within 15 days of  receipt of such result;
 (c) Upon such request being made if compelling and exceptional  circumstances exist, Special Court may permit retesting of samples  after recording cogent reasons in the order;
 (d) No application for retesting shall be entertained after expiry of 15 days  or in the absence of compelling circumstances;
